{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WuKongIM/WuKongIM/pulls/1024","id":4956525987,"node_id":"PR_kwDOJgfwyc8AAAABJ26Vow","html_url":"https://github.com/WuKongIM/WuKongIM/pull/1024","diff_url":"https://github.com/WuKongIM/WuKongIM/pull/1024.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/WuKongIM/WuKongIM/pull/1024.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WuKongIM/WuKongIM/issues/1024","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WuKongIM/WuKongIM/pulls/1024/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WuKongIM/WuKongIM/pulls/1024/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WuKongIM/WuKongIM/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WuKongIM/WuKongIM/issues/1024/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WuKongIM/WuKongIM/statuses/f419ea8f82c8bd16a777cfc3bf6cbf8c85be60dd","number":1024,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"fix(scripts): retain terminal diagnostics and join cancelled profiles","user":{"login":"tangtaoit","id":3895878,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM4OTU4Nzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3895878?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tangtaoit","html_url":"https://github.com/tangtaoit","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tangtaoit/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tangtaoit/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tangtaoit/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tangtaoit/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tangtaoit/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tangtaoit/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tangtaoit/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tangtaoit/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tangtaoit/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Cloud RC failures could lose worker failure samples and terminal status, discard oversized metric results, or query a window after the workload stopped. This retains bounded terminal diagnostics, partitions fixed metric queries under shared time/byte limits, and anchors their window to the terminal report. Missing or partial evidence stays explicit and never changes the workload verdict.\n\nThe full regression also exposed a profile-helper cancellation race: a signal between starting curl and registering its PID could leave a request alive after interruption was reported. Cleanup is now deferred through complete PID/file registration, then cancels and joins owned requests. Empty cleanup arrays work under Bash 3 nounset. Test fixtures preserve all assertions while eliminating unnecessary subprocess/build work; one real-process Start case moves into the integration tier.\n\nTests were written and failed before the fixes. Local terminal collection covers 20 methods / 79 process scenarios. Nine deterministic signal scenarios exercise prelaunch and first/second-node registration with HUP/INT/TERM. The direct-lab differential confirms two unused builds disappear while the full operation, artifact, permission and state assertions remain. Independent Standards and Spec reviews of each source increment have no blocking findings.\n\nFirst complete CI for f419ea8f passed at checkout 0c575fd63bcf8164332ca28053039f8fdf84137f, same tree a13367b2dc4658e6c27a1992f240544636e5178d. Candidate run 39670542965 attempt 1 passed the default suite (219 packages), original full scripts command (576.017 seconds; 651 top-level PASS, six existing SKIP), five migration topologies / 55 history checks, cross-node delivery and single-/three-node self-chat. Terminal-retention and all cancellation cases completed. All six owned process sessions were independently verified clear. Linux inner collector case-by-case JSON was not uploaded; completion is established through its enclosing named regression.\n\nPerformance run 39670542860 attempt 1 passed all nine measurement windows (270,000 planned/started/completed, zero errors/drops) and the 90-second correctness smoke. One internal retry and transport rejection remain recorded; the captured mixed trace has incomplete flight counters. These results do not prove an exclusive-host baseline or long-duration qualification.\n\nEarlier first-run failures remain retained: c91e37b4 hit the 600-second outer deadline; 2cc562fa completed but exposed the cancellation assertion; 44de9452 hit the same outer deadline without an assertion failure. No failed head was rerun, no limit or concurrency setting was relaxed, and no test was filtered from the Linux gate. Timing analysis establishes little budget margin, not a unique runner cause.\n\nThe cloud message-loss root cause remains unconfirmed. This is diagnostic retention and cancellation cleanup, not a claimed repair of that loss. Product cmd/internal/pkg and dependency objects remain unchanged. No cloud resources, production keys, stable activation or release publication are included.\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-21T18:36:21Z","updated_at":"2026-10-21T20:44:42Z","closed_at":"2026-10-21T20:44:41Z","merged_at":"2026-10-21T20:44:41Z","merge_commit_sha":"79a7177032a6ae1ec7015cefe0e6f94eb0f19f06","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"WuKongIM:codex/v3-rc-terminal-evidence","ref":"codex/v3-rc-terminal-evidence","repo":{"id":638054601,"node_id":"R_kgDOJgfwyQ","name":"WuKongIM","full_name":"WuKongIM/WuKongIM","owner":{"login":"WuKongIM","id":132860831,"node_id":"O_kgDOB-tLnw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/132860831?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WuKongIM","html_url":"https://github.com/WuKongIM","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WuKongIM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WuKongIM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WuKongIM/gis